"""BarrelViewer: our barrel boxes on the robot's camera, live (Dave's ask, 2026-11-03).

Once a second: take the robot's current image, run the detector as it stands (frozen v1 segmentation +
the stripe-anchored detector, barrels.worldmap_bridge.BarrelDetectorHook.default()), show the result in
a window. Nothing downstream of the picture is touched: the world map still uses the vendor detector.

Run (robot on, setup.zsh sourced, docs/RUNBOOK.md):

    cd barrels/live
    genfsm BarrelViewer.fsm          # writes BarrelViewer.py next to this file (only needed after editing the .fsm)
    simple_cli BarrelViewer          # connects to $ROBOT and starts the machine

At the C> prompt:  tm seg    -> show the color segmentation blended over the image
                   tm boxes  -> show the boxes (the default; yellow = orange barrel, green = blue)
                   tm both   -> both
Quit with Ctrl+\\ before powering the robot off.

The state machine is two nodes: ShowFrame grabs and shows a frame, SetMode switches the view. `loop`
re-enters ShowFrame every second (=T(1)=>); a text message (=TM('seg')=> etc.) detours through SetMode and
comes straight back (=N=>). All the image work is in the hook, so the photo path (tools/detect_image.py)
and this program run exactly the same code; robot.camera_image is RGB, imshow wants RGB, the hook converts
to OpenCV's BGR and back inside.
"""
from aim_fsm import *
from barrels import worldmap_bridge as wb


class BarrelViewer(StateMachineProgram):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__(aruco=False, particle_filter=False, speech=False,
                         launch_cam_viewer=False, launch_worldmap_viewer=False)
        self.hook = wb.BarrelDetectorHook.default()   # frozen v1 model + the stripe detector + provisional camera
        self.mode = "boxes"
        self.last_count = None

    class ShowFrame(StateNode):
        def start(self, event=None):
            super().start(event)
            program = self.parent
            image = self.robot.camera_image
            if image is None:
                print("BarrelViewer: no camera image yet")
                return
            imshow("barrels", program.hook.view(image, program.mode))
            n = len(program.hook.last_barrels)
            if n != program.last_count:        # one line when the count changes, not every second
                names = ", ".join(b.color_name for b in program.hook.last_barrels) or "none"
                print(f"BarrelViewer: {n} barrel{'s' if n != 1 else ''} ({names})")
                program.last_count = n

    class SetMode(StateNode):
        def __init__(self, mode):
            super().__init__()
            self.mode = mode

        def start(self, event=None):
            super().start(event)
            self.parent.mode = self.mode
            print(f"BarrelViewer: showing {self.mode}")

    $setup{
        loop: self.ShowFrame() =T(1)=> loop
        loop =TM('boxes')=> self.SetMode('boxes') =N=> loop
        loop =TM('seg')=> self.SetMode('seg') =N=> loop
        loop =TM('both')=> self.SetMode('both') =N=> loop
    }
